    "Where to cut the first packet. A number is a byte offset; markers: method, host, endhost, sld (the site name), midsld (its middle), endsld, sniext (the TLS server-name field). Add +N or -N." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {}
    },
    "While it is on, iOS turns the bypass back on by itself after a dropped connection or a network change. Turning it off in Zapret, Control Center, or Shortcuts stops it until you turn it on again." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {}
    },
    "While sharing is on, anyone on this Wi-Fi network can use this iPhone's bypass. Use an app that supports SOCKS5 proxies on the other device and enter this address there. Turn the bypass on to start sharing." : {
